Introduction to Data Lake and Limitations

Delta Lake - is a file format

Data Lake :
Data lake is a storage repository that holds vast amount of data of raw in is native format.
Data lake store all the data in the form of files.
It can hold any kind of data.
Eg: S3, ADLS Gen2, GCS
Data lake is mainly built on object storage, all the above examples are also object storage.

Advantages of Data Lake : 
	- Cost effective
	- Scalable
	- Stores any  kind of data.
		Structured - CSV
		Semi  - JSON
		Unstructured - image,audio & log

Challenges of Data Lake :
	- No ACID guarantee
		we need ACID guarantee when we perform transactions.
		Any database will provide ACID guarantee
		
		ACID --
			Atomicity
			Consistency
			Isolation
			Durability

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


Why Data Lake lack ACID guarantee


Example:
When we run a spark job 10 multiple tasks underneath and each generate a part file..

Scenario 1 -  A job failed while appending the data

we already have output folder with 5 part files and the current job generates 5 part files, so total is 10.

2 files are generated and job failed in mid
current total now 7 part files.

The reader will read 7 files

Here Atomicity and Consistency did met 

For Atomicity we need 10 files
and Consistency then 2 generated files should be cleared


Scenario 2 - Job failed while overwriting the data

Overwrite is a 2 step process.
	1.Delete what is already present
	2.Write the new data / files

5 part files are already present in the output older and after we ran the job, 2 files are generated and in the mid job fails.

Here 
	Atomicity 
	Consistency
	Durability 
did not meet 


Scenario 3 - Simultaneous Reads and Writes

5 part files are already available  and then you invoked the spark job
2 part files are written 

and now reader is trying to read while part file 3 is getting processed.

Currently Reader can see 7 files

Here Isolation is lost, 
cause until all the data is written none should have been read


Scenario 4 - Append the data with a different Schema

5 part files are present with each file having 5 columns 

Current running job will write 5 more part files, but these new files ave 7 col

Total - 10 files
5 files - 5 columns each
5 files - 7 columns each

When a reader starts reading then whatever the file it reads first then it will assume all the files have same cols

if  5 col file is read then it will assume all files have 5 col each and it is same for the other files



So with Data lake,
It may lead to Data Reliability issues, Data Quality issues.
There is no Data validation
The above scenarios leads data corruption in failure scenarios
No DML (Update and Delete)operation as ACID properties are not available
Difficult to maintain historical versions


For all the above problems can be overcome by Delta lake 

