Introduction to Delta Lake**

Delta lake - is an open source storage layer
it is like a small utility installed on your spark cluster.


Parquet format
	- It is a column based file format
	- Very will used with Apache spark
	- It embeds the metadata

Delta is combination of Parquet and Transaction logs

Delta -> Parquet + Transaction logs.

If in 5 tasks are running, then
in delta
	5 part files (parquet) will be created in output folder
	along with another folder will be created  - _delta_logs
		inside this folder **Transaction** entities will be held like metadata,whether file has been added or deleted or updated
			this folder contains  0000.json files

For Performing actions in Delta lake

**Write Operation:**

5 parquet files written and 1 transaction file

part-000.parquet
part-001.parquet
part-002.parquet
part-003.parquet
part-004.parquet

_delta_log
0000.json

Only when all the files are written to the output folder then transction file _delta_log is written making it is successful.


**Append Operation:**

2 part files are getting appended
part-005.parquet
part-006.parquet

_delta_log
00001.json

The transaction file is generated only when 2 files are completely written
Here 7 part files and 2 transaction files


For each Write operation:
	All part files are written first
	A Transaction log is added to _delta_log folder (JSON format)

For each Read operation:
	Transaction log files are read first
	Part files are read based on the data present in log files.
Transaction files will have the data which are the ones updated, inserted files, this will determine which needed to be read and part files are read accordingly

